<title>BELGIUM: Belgian October car registrations up 8.8% yr-on-yr.</title>
<headline>Belgian October car registrations up 8.8% yr-on-yr.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian new car registrations rose 8.8 percent in October compared with the same year ago period, the Belgian Automotive Industry Association, known as Febiac, said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Registrations were up 13.0 percent in the year to date compared with the same 1995 period. Febiac said also that nine-month registrations in 1996, a motor show year, were up 3.4 percent on those for 1994, the year the last show was held.</p>
<p>    BELGIAN CAR REGISTRATIONS  Oct 96	  Oct 95</p>
<p>    Month			   32,635	  30,009</p>
<p>    Cumulative Jan-Oct	 355,894	 314,838</p>
<p>October registrations by manufacturer and market share for those above three percent versus 1995 period.</p>
<p> VW	6,258 (19.2 pct)  vs   5,580 (18.6 pct)</p>
<p> Peugeot 5,182 (15.9 pct)  vs   5,163 (17.2 pct)</p>
<p> GM	3,444 (10.6 pct)  vs   2,570 ( 8.6 pct)</p>
<p> Renault 3,393 (10.4 pct)  vs   3,668 (12.2 pct)</p>
<p> Ford    2,335 ( 7.2 pct)  vs   2,331 ( 7.8 pct)</p>
<p> BMW     1,675 ( 5.1 pct)  vs   1,460 ( 4.9 pct)</p>
<p> Toyota  1,617 ( 5.0 pct)  vs   1,409 ( 4.7 pct)</p>
<p> Fiat    1,512 ( 4.6 pct)  vs   1,131 ( 3.8 pct)</p>
<p> Nissan  1,348 ( 4.1 pct)  vs   1,321 ( 4.4 pct)</p>
<p> Volvo   1,139 ( 3.5 pct)  vs     781 ( 2.6 pct)</p>
<p> Mercedes  1,105 ( 3.4 pct)  vs     904 ( 3.0 pct)</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
